riscos-mesa: the Raspberry Pi's hello_triangle examples, rebuilt
=================================================================

These are two of the Raspberry Pi's own hello_pi examples, rebuilt from
source against riscos-mesa (EGL, OpenGL ES and the DispmanX compatibility
library). They show that existing Pi Khronos programs port to riscos-mesa.
They run on any RISC OS 5 machine, the Pi 4 included.

Needs SharedUnixLibrary and ARMEABISupport (the !Run files load them from
System:Modules if they aren't loaded already).

Like the originals they draw over the whole screen and don't multitask.
The desktop is redrawn when they exit.

!HelloTriangle   spinning cube with three photo textures (OpenGL ES 1.1).
                 Press any key to exit.
!HelloTriangle2  Julia set over a Mandelbrot set (OpenGL ES 2.0 shaders).
                 Move the mouse to change it; click Menu to exit.
                 The shaders run on the CPU, so it renders about 320
                 pixels wide and scales that up to the screen.
                 *Set HelloTriangle2$Scale N renders at 1/N of the screen
                 size instead (lower N: sharper and slower).

Please report: whether the textures show on the cube, whether the fractals
follow the mouse, and roughly how many frames a second each manages.

The sources and the notes on porting other Pi programs are in
ports/hello_pi in the riscos-mesa repository. Licence: BSD (the Raspberry
Pi userland licence, in each application's Licence file).
